---
import { INSTALL_COMMANDS, LINKS, LINUX_FONT_COMMAND } from '../config';
---

<section class="section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
  <div class="container req">
    <div>
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="section-kicker">Requirements</p>
        <h2 class="section-title" id="install-title">Before you tune in</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="req__list">
        <li>
          <strong>macOS 14 or later</strong>, Apple Silicon or Intel: Apple Music and your local music files, side by
          side.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>An Apple Music subscription</strong> for the catalog, on macOS. The first launch asks for Apple Music
          access.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Or Linux</strong>, x86_64 or ARM64 with glibc: your local music files only (Apple Music needs macOS).
          Sound goes through PulseAudio, PipeWire or ALSA.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Local files</strong>: mp3, flac, ogg and wav from <code>~/Music</code> or the folders
          in <code>music_dirs</code>. See <a href={LINKS.localFiles} rel="noopener">local files</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A terminal</strong> of 80×24 or larger. Set its font to Kode Mono for the intended look.
        </li>
        <li>
          Optional, on macOS: independent app volume needs macOS 14.2+; the live spectrum behind the rain for Apple
          Music needs macOS 15+.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="req__note">Not affiliated with Apple.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="req__steps">
      <h3>Install on macOS</h3>
      <pre><code><span class="c"># signed, notarized; installs Kode Mono</span>
{INSTALL_COMMANDS.macos}
nu11signal</code></pre>
      <h3>Install on Linux</h3>
      <pre><code><span class="c"># Homebrew on Linux, then the font</span>
{INSTALL_COMMANDS.linux}
{LINUX_FONT_COMMAND}
nu11signal</code></pre>
      <p>
        Or install a <code>linux-amd64</code> or <code>linux-arm64</code> release archive; see
        the <a href={LINKS.installLinux} rel="noopener">Linux install guide</a>.
      </p>
      <h3>No subscription handy?</h3>
      <p>Point it at your music files, or build from source and try the UI against a simulated player:</p>
      <pre><code>make demo</code></pre>
      <p>
        Release archives for a manual install on either platform are on <a href={LINKS.releases} rel="noopener">GitHub Releases</a>. See
        the <a href={LINKS.docs} rel="noopener">documentation</a> for building, usage and troubleshooting.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .req {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 22rem), 1fr));
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }
  .req__list {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .req__list li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.5rem 0 0.5rem 1.75rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  .req__list li::before {
    content: '▸';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.25rem;
    color: var(--accent-text);
  }
  .req__list strong,
  .req__list code,
  .req__steps p code {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .req__list code,
  .req__steps p code {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .req__note {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .req__steps h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    color: var(--cyan);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }
  .req__steps h3:not(:first-child) {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }
  .req__steps p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--dim);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--yellow);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  pre .c {
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
</style>
